# Single-page-app fallback.
#
# The router is a BrowserRouter, so /applications, /certificates, /chat and
# every other route exist only in the browser - there is no such file on the
# static host. Without this rule, a refresh or a pasted deep link returns the
# host's own 404 page instead of the app. Netlify and Render Static Sites both
# read this file; the 200 (not 301) keeps the URL the user actually requested.
/*    /index.html   200
